# Always deploy API changes

When you add or change **backend/API code** (`app/api/**`, `lib/**` used by routes, Supabase migrations, server middleware), **deployment is part of the task** — not optional and not something to ask the user about.

## Do automatically (no "say the word" / "deploy when ready")

1. Branch off latest `main`.
2. Run `npm run typecheck` (and `npm run build` for app-facing changes).
3. Open a PR with a clear summary + test plan.
4. **Merge when CI is green** (squash + delete branch).
5. **Verify live** on `main` via `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shashank4910/JobRadar/main/<path>`.

## Do not

- End a task with "deploy the API changes" or "say the word to ship" for backend work you wrote.
- Leave API fixes only on a local branch or an open PR.
- Ask "should I merge?" when CI is green.

## Extension-only changes

Extension JS/CSS still ships via the same PR to `main` (repo source of truth). Tell the user to reload the extension at `chrome://extensions` after merge — that is the one manual step they must do locally.

## Pause before merge only when

- CI is red (fix first).
- User explicitly said "don't merge yet" or "PR only".
- Merge would require force-push to `main`.
